  "payload": {
    "rawResponseText": "Hotel owners who want **brand affiliation** but still want to preserve a stronger sense of **individuality** commonly look at **soft brands** and **lifestyle/boutique-style brands** such as **Autograph Collection**, **The Luxury Collection**, **Curio Collection**, **Vignette Collection**, **Kimpton**, **Hotel Indigo**, **W Hotels**, **Moxy**, **Edition**, **Alila**, **Unbound Collection**, and **Radisson Individuals**.[4][12][19][7]\n\nThese brands are designed to keep more of a hotel’s own character, local design, and independent-feeling identity while still giving access to a parent company’s distribution system, loyalty program, and standards.[4][12][19][7]\n\nCommonly cited examples include:\n- **Marriott**: Autograph Collection, The Luxury Collection, Edition, Moxy[4][1]\n- **IHG**: Kimpton, Hotel Indigo, Vignette Collection, Six Senses[3][15][12]\n- **Hyatt**: Alila, Unbound Collection, Destination Hotels, JdV by Hyatt[11][12][17]\n- **Hilton**: Curio Collection, LXR, Canopy[12][19]\n- **Accor**: 25hours, 21c Museum Hotels[2][16]\n- **Choice/Radisson-related positioning**: Radisson Individuals[7]\n\nIf you want, I can also narrow this to the **best-known luxury soft brands** or the **best options for upscale/select-service owners**.",
